[51.06584, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[H\r\u001b[2B\u001b[38;5;231m\u25cf\u001b[3G\u001b[39m\u001b[1m\ud83d\udcac bob\u001b[22m\u001b[K\r\u001b[2B \u001b[3G\u001b[1m\ud83d\udce5\u001b[10G\u001b[22m\u00b7\u001b[12Gearlier\r\u001b[2C\u001b[2B\u001b[2m\u258e\u001b[22m \u001b[3mHi! Quick question about customer-churn-v3: are the train/test splits grouped by customer_id, or\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[23m\u001b[2m\u258e\u001b[5G\u001b[22m\u001b[3msplit row-wise? I need to rule out cross-split leakage before I start training. Thanks!\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[23m\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[1m\ud83d\udce4 you\u001b[22m \u00b7 now\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[2B\u001b[2m\u258e\u001b[22m \u001b[3mv3 is row-wise random split (70/15/15), NOT grouped by customer_id \u2014 same customer can appear in\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[23m\u001b[2m\u258e\u001b[5G\u001b[22m\u001b[3mtrain/val/test, so it leaks for per-customer models. Use customer-churn-v3.1 instead: same \r\u001b[4C\u001b[1Bschema/rows but GroupShuffleSplit on customer_id (70/15/15), no customer cro\u001b[82Gses splits.\u001b[23m\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1BReply sent. Wake monitor still armed for bob's next message.\u001b[K\r\u001b[2B\u001b[38;5;246m\u273b\u001b[3GChurned for 11s \u00b7 2 monitors still running\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[2B\u001b[38;5;231m\u25cf\u001b[3G\u001b[39mMonitor event: \"Wake monitor for alice's inbox\u001b[50G\u2014\u001b[52Gdetects\u001b[60Gnew\u001b[64Gmessag"]
[51.065916, "o", "es\u001b[73Gfrom\u001b[78Gbob\"\r\u001b[2B\u001b[38;5;246m \u001b[3G\u001b[39mRu\u001b[6Gning\u001b[11G\u001b[1m1\u001b[22m shell command\u2026\u001b[K\u001b[30;1H\u001b[28;3H\u001b[?25h"]
